// E2E for ADR 0130 / BT-3715: class variables live in the class process.
// A block reads and writes its home class's variables only at home; abroad
// it reads the value captured at creation and a write raises
// `class_state_unreachable`. Boundaries (on:do:) discard what happened
// inside them. Driven through the REPL protocol because the feature crosses
// compile, load, the class gen_server and error display (ADR 0069 lesson,
// docs/development/testing-strategy.md section 8). BUnit coverage:
// stdlib/test/class_var_semantics_*_test.bt.
//
// Error assertions are substrings of what the REPL actually prints (the
// structured kind is not in the display; the message text is). Abroad write:
// runtime `class_state_unreachable`; performLocally: write: `class_state_read_only`.
// No display behaviour is changed or specified here.
//
// Class names are prefixed Cvsh* to stay unique in the shared workspace.

// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_counter.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_loud.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_ids.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_tally.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_tally_main.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_probe.bt
// @load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_probechild.bt

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The ADR's Counter / LoudCounter example: loop-body writes and a stored
// closure invoked within the same invocation both take effect at home.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshCounter run
// => 2

CvshLoudCounter run
// => 3

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// on:do: is a catch boundary: the write inside the protected body is
// discarded when the error is caught; a write made before it is kept.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshIds tryTake
// => 0

CvshIds next
// => 0

CvshIds tryTakeKeepingEarlierWrite
// => 1

CvshIds tryTakeKeepingEarlierWrite
// => 2

CvshIds next
// => 0

// Uncaught, the same error surfaces to the REPL.
CvshIds take
// => ERROR: boom

CvshIds next
// => 0

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A block carried synchronously into another class's class method (the
// callee has class state, so it runs in its own process). A read sees the
// live value (the home is blocked, so captured == live); a write raises.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshTally readViaBatch
// => 5

CvshTally writeViaBatch
// => ERROR: class variable total cannot be read from this process

// The uncaught error discards the whole invocation's writes, including the
// reset made before the failed write, so the earlier 5 is unchanged.
CvshTally total
// => 5

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Stored closures. Run from a later invocation of the same class they are at
// home: live read, write succeeds.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshTally reset
// => 0

bumper := CvshTally makeBumper
// => _

CvshTally run: bumper
// => 1

CvshTally total
// => 1

reader := CvshTally makeReader
// => _

CvshTally add: 4
// => 5

CvshTally run: reader
// => 5

// Run from the REPL process, after the invocation ended: the read answers the
// value captured when the block was made (1), and the write raises.
reader value
// => 1

bumper value
// => ERROR: class variable total cannot be read from this process

CvshTally total
// => 5

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// performLocally: runs the method in the caller against a read-only snapshot
// of the last completed state: reads work, writes raise class_state_read_only.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshTally performLocally: #total withArguments: #()
// => 5

CvshTally performLocally: #add: withArguments: #(1)
// => ERROR: class variable total is read-only here

CvshTally total
// => 5

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Unsealed parent / stateful subclass: hasField: follows the receiver.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

CvshProbeBase probe
// => false

CvshProbeChild probe
// => true

CvshProbeBase probeInBlock
// => false

CvshProbeChild probeInBlock
// => true

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Hot reload of a class with classState: mid-session keeps its map.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_reload_v1.bt
// => Loaded: CvshReload

CvshReload bump
// => 1

CvshReload bump
// => 2

:load tests/repl-protocol/fixtures/class_var_single_home_reload_v2.bt
// => Loaded: CvshReload

CvshReload n
// => 2

CvshReload bump
// => 12
